## Overview

This vignette is to explore Rotten Tomatoes' Tomatometer, which is an aggregate from critics' ratings on the site, and how it compares with the Popcornmeter, which in contrast is an aggregate from general users of the site's ratings.

```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(
  collapse = TRUE,
  comment = "#>"
)
```

## Setup

```{r setup, warning=FALSE}
library(pixarfilms)
library(dplyr)
library(tidyr)
library(ggtext)
library(ggplot2)
library(extrafont)
```


## Wrangle data

```{r}
# Make data long for easier plotting
rt_tbl_long <-
  rt_tbl |>
  mutate(critics_review = as.numeric(critics_review),
	 audience_review = as.numeric(audience_review)) |>
  mutate(film = fct_reorder(film, critics_review)) |>  # Order by critics
  pivot_longer(cols = c(critics_review, audience_review),
	       names_to = "review")

# Split out data
critics <- rt_tbl_long |>
  filter(review == "critics_review")
audience <- rt_tbl_long |>
  filter(review == "audience_review")
```


